SKEPTIC REVIEW RAW DATA — "retired-instruction count as bit-exact measure of
inference work" candidate (INSTRUMENT angle)
Date: 2026-07-29
Reviewer lens: so-who-cares
Box: dev Chromebook, Intel i5-10210U (Comet Lake) under crosvm, 8 vCPU.
     /sys/devices/cpu/caps/pmu_name = skylake
Binary: ./aegis-linux/target/release/aegis-linux (built 2026-07-16 22:58, UNMODIFIED)
Model:  model-lab/tinybit/m7_final_gate_work/artifacts/{MODEL.SAF,EMBED.BIN,VOCAB.BIN}
Prompt: "Once upon a time", max_new_tokens 16
Tool:   valgrind-3.24.0, installed from Debian archive this session (apt candidate
        1:3.24.0-3). NO PMU, NO MSR access, NO privileges, NO bare metal used.

CLAIM UNDER TEST (candidate's "WHY ONLY HERE" pillar, quoted verbatim):
  "The bit-exactness is the whole claim and it is structurally unavailable under
   an OS: a hosted process accrues a variable number of retired instructions from
   context switches, page faults, ASLR-dependent code paths, dynamic-loader work
   and syscall entry, so INST_RETIRED for a fixed workload is a distribution, not
   a constant."
VERDICT: MEASURED FALSE. See below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
ARM A — cachegrind, WHOLE PROCESS (loader + startup + file I/O included)
  valgrind --tool=cachegrind --cache-sim=no --branch-sim=no
  run1 (load ~1):     322,008,993 Ir
  run2 (load 7.38):   322,024,728 Ir
  run3 (load ~10):    322,024,475 Ir
  run4 (load 12.80):  322,028,480 Ir
  n=4  range 19,487 Ir = 0.0061% of total   CV 0.0027%
  Residual is process startup (loader/env/argv), NOT the compute region.

ARM B — callgrind, BRACKETED to the compute region only
  valgrind --tool=callgrind --collect-atstart=no
           --toggle-collect='*forward_step*' --cache-sim=no --branch-sim=no
  (this is exactly the "bracket only the pure compute region" the candidate
   states is a hard requirement for its own bare-metal measurement)
  run1 (load 11.17):  243,199,887 Ir
  run2 (load 11.17):  243,199,887 Ir
  run3 (load 11.17):  243,199,887 Ir
  run4 (later, idle): 243,199,887 Ir
  n=4  range 0 Ir.  BIT-EXACT, TO THE UNIT, 4/4.
  Achieved under load average 11.17 on 8 vCPU, inside a crosvm guest, with
  ASLR on, page cache cold/warm mixed, 12 competing spinner processes.

COST — callgrind wall 1.88 s vs native wall 0.06 s = 31.9x slowdown.
  Total engineering to obtain the above: one apt install + two CLI flags.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THE CANDIDATE'S PREMISE FAILS
  The candidate conflates "PMU instruction counts are nondeterministic under an
  OS" (TRUE, and the rr project's documented battle) with "instruction counts are
  nondeterministic under an OS" (FALSE). You do not need the PMU to count
  instructions. Valgrind counts them in software by simulation, which is
  deterministic by construction and immune to every noise source the candidate
  lists: context switches, page faults, ASLR, loader work and syscall entry all
  occur OUTSIDE the bracketed region and are simply not counted.

PRIOR ART THIS PUTS THE CANDIDATE BEHIND (all pre-existing, all mature)
  - Valgrind cachegrind/callgrind: bit-exact instruction counts since 2002.
  - rust-lang/rustc-perf uses instruction counts as its PRIMARY metric precisely
    because they are noise-resistant; cachegrind is configured there with
    --cache-sim=no because "99% of the time instruction counts are all you need."
  - iai-callgrind: a Rust bench harness whose stated purpose is "accurate
    measurements even in virtualized CI environments, completely negating the
    noise of the environment." Drops into aegis-core/benches/ next to the
    existing Criterion benches.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
COROLLARY CLAIM ("SMM instruction tax needs no OS") — ALSO FAILS
  /sys/devices/cpu/freeze_on_smi  EXISTS on this box and READS 1.
  i.e. Linux perf exposes IA32_DEBUGCTL[14] FREEZE_WHILE_SMM as a supported
  sysfs knob, and the kernel already defaults it ON for Comet Lake and later
  (upstream patch: "x86/perf: Default freeze_on_smi on for Comet Lake and later").
  The bit the candidate proposes to reach via a hand-rolled IDT + ring-0 MSR
  write on a 2015 Dell is already flipped, by the OS, on the dev box.
  Availability gate is ALSO mis-specified by the candidate: FREEZE_WHILE_SMM is
  supported only if IA32_PERF_CAPABILITIES(0x345)[12] == 1. The proposed Stage-0
  CPUID.0AH probe does not test for it at all.
  Metric is the wrong one: SMM steals TIME (plus a cache flush). Instruction
  count of the SMI handler measures firmware code volume, not workload cost.
  Delgado & Karavanic, "Performance Implications of System Management Mode,"
  IISWC 2013 — the candidate's own named venue — already characterized SMM
  performance impact at application/system/hypervisor level using TSC deltas
  and controlled SMI injection.
  Candidate's own confound (3) is a documented real failure:
  microsoft/WSL issue #7951 "IA32_DEBUGCTL.FREEZE_WHILE_SMM does not appear to
  be honored."

--------------------------------------------------------------------
PAYOFF ARTIFACT IS ALSO UNREACHABLE AS SCOPED
  Promised artifact: "pshufb executes 0.71x the instructions at 0.61x the IPC;
  the loss is entirely a port-pressure/latency effect on Broadwell."
  Instructions + IPC CANNOT establish port pressure. That requires per-port uop
  distribution (UOPS_DISPATCHED_PORT.PORT_n across 8 ports = 4 GP counters +
  event multiplexing + IA32_PERFEVTSELx programming), which the candidate does
  not scope — it scopes FIXED_CTR0 = INST_RETIRED only.
  The quantity is instead obtainable STATICALLY and FREE: llvm-mca reports
  per-port resource pressure and bottlenecks for Broadwell/Skylake from the
  assembly; uiCA (Abel & Reineke, 2022) and uops.info are the accepted method.
  Neither needs hardware, an IDT, or a boot.
  And the promised inversion ("would win on a machine with a wider shuffle port")
  cannot be DEMONSTRATED on this program's fleet: Broadwell-U and Goldmont Plus
  only. No Ice Lake, no Zen, no wider-shuffle machine exists to test on.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
CROSS-REFERENCE — the premise was already dead from the other side
  docs/hardware_logs/skeptic_variance_budget_kill_2026-07-29.log establishes,
  from the same program's own data:
   - between-launch variance on pinned quiesced Linux is indistinguishable from
     ZERO (B^2 = -0.881); residual is iid per-step jitter averaging as 1/sqrt(N).
   - resolving a 16% effect at 95%/80% needs 72 decode steps = ~0.2 s/arm.
   - resolving a 3% effect needs ~4.7 s/arm.
   - the bare-metal "CV 0.078%, 7 repeats" is 7 replicates of ONE 33-token
     prefill in which DECODE EMITTED ZERO TOKENS; the honest pinned-Linux vs
     bare-metal-decode ratio is 3x, not 100-200x.
  So the OS noise floor is not larger than the effects to be explained. It is
  ~100x smaller after 0.2 seconds of averaging.

BOTTOM LINE: the candidate spends a multi-day IDT + ring-0 MSR budget, on a
machine cpu.rs:163-165 warns can be bricked by exactly those writes, to obtain
a number this log obtained in 15 minutes with `apt install valgrind`, at higher
precision (0 Ir range vs the bare-metal arm's 0.078-0.105% TSC CV and 0.2%
cross-boot drift), on the noisiest box the program owns.
